Imagine that you have the following function:

function findSmallest(num1, num2){
    if(num1 < num2){
        return num1;
    } else {
        return num2;
    }
}

What information does the user need to know in order to use this function if it were included in a library of functions? To write an API for this function, you need to include how the function works, all the parameters and their data types with a short description of each, and what (if anything) will be returned. The API for the function could be this:

findSmallest: Given two numbers, finds the smallest
num1 {number} - first number 
num2 {number} - second number
return {number} - the smaller of the two numbers

Which topic interests you more: testing a function or procedural abstraction?
